  "description": "meme-id: cheers_to_all_the_people; hasOverallIntent: Propaganda; overall-intent-description: The image shows a smiling woman holding a glass of champagne, with text that reads: 'cheers to all the people who can change their minds when presented with information that contradicts their beliefs.' The overall intent is to use the positive, celebratory visual of a toast to frame the concept of being open-minded or intellectually flexible as something to be celebrated. This is a form of propaganda, as it aims to influence the viewer's perception by associating the desirable trait of being open to changing one's mind with a festive, socially acceptable image. The meme does not contain any toxic elements such as abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or discriminatory content against any protected group. The intent is to promote the value of intellectual humility and adaptability in the face of new information, using the visual metaphor of a toast to make the message more palatable and engaging.",
